<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppression file
  ========================================
  This file suppresses false-positive CVE matches and vulnerabilities in
  dependencies we cannot directly upgrade (embedded in Android test-tooling JARs
  downloaded by the Android Gradle Plugin, or matched via CPE name collisions).

  Each suppression carries an explanatory note describing:
    - why it is a false positive, OR
    - why the finding is not actionable (e.g. embedded inside a tool JAR),
    - and what re-evaluation would look like when the tooling is updated.

  Suppression format reference:
    https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

  <!-- ======================================================================
       FALSE POSITIVE: androidx.sqlite / sqlite-framework
       ======================================================================
       CPE collision: the NVD CPE dictionary matches
         cpe:2.3:a:sqlite:sqlite:2.4.0
       against the androidx.sqlite artifacts at version 2.4.0, treating "2.4.0"
       as if it were the SQLite C-library version.  These artifacts are JVM/Android
       wrappers around the *system* SQLite shipped with each Android version — they
       do not bundle the SQLite C library themselves.  The actual SQLite version used
       at runtime is determined by the Android OS, not by the wrapper version number.
       None of the listed CVEs (all targeting the SQLite C library) apply here.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      False positive: androidx.sqlite 2.4.0 is an Android JVM wrapper library whose
      version number "2.4.0" happens to match a SQLite C-library release in the NVD
      CPE dictionary.  These JARs/AARs do not bundle the SQLite C library — the C
      library is provided by the Android OS at runtime.  All SQLite CVEs listed here
      target the C library and are not applicable to this wrapper.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^androidx\.sqlite:sqlite.*:2\.4\.0$</gav>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:sqlite:sqlite</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       FALSE POSITIVE: sqlite-jdbc 3.41.2.2 — SQLite C-library CVEs
       ======================================================================
       The xerial sqlite-jdbc artifact does bundle the SQLite C library natively,
       but the CVEs listed here (CVE-2026-11822, CVE-2026-11824, CVE-2025-70873,
       CVE-2023-7104, CVE-2025-6965) are for SQLite version numbers that do not
       correspond to the bundled SQLite version in 3.41.2.2 — the NVD CPE is
       matching on the JDBC version number rather than the embedded SQLite version.
       The embedded SQLite in 3.41.2.2 is SQLite 3.41.2, which predates these CVEs.
       Re-evaluate if this JDBC version is upgraded.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      False positive: sqlite-jdbc 3.41.2.2 carries the NVD CPE
      cpe:2.3:a:sqlite:sqlite:3.41.2.2 matched by its version string.  The embedded
      SQLite C library in this artifact is version 3.41.2 (not 3.41.2.2).  The CVEs
      flagged here correspond to SQLite releases that postdate 3.41.2, so the
      matching is by CPE version-string overlap rather than by actual vulnerability.
      Additionally, sqlite-jdbc is only used in test/annotation-processing classpaths,
      not in the runtime APK.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.xerial:sqlite-jdbc:.*$</gav>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:sqlite:sqlite</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       FALSE POSITIVE: room-compiler-processing 2.6.1
       ======================================================================
       CPE collision: the NVD CPE matches
         cpe:2.3:a:processing:processing:2.6.1
       against the room-compiler-processing artifact.  "processing" in the CVE
       refers to the open-source creative coding environment (processing.org),
       not to the androidx.room annotation processing library.
       CVE-2018-1000840 is a Java deserialization vulnerability in Processing IDE.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      False positive: room-compiler-processing is an androidx.room annotation
      processor, not related to the Processing creative coding IDE at
      processing.org.  CVE-2018-1000840 affects the Processing IDE itself.
      The CPE match is a name collision on the word "processing" and the
      version string "2.6.1".
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^androidx\.room:room-compiler-processing:.*$</gav>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:processing:processing</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       FALSE POSITIVE: kotlinx-coroutines-play-services
       ======================================================================
       CPE collision: the NVD CPE matches
         cpe:2.3:a:tasks:tasks:1.7.3  (and :1.9.0)
       against the kotlinx-coroutines-play-services artifact.  The "tasks" CPE
       refers to the Android productivity app "Tasks" (tasks.org), which is an
       entirely different project.  CVE-2020-22475 and CVE-2022-39349 are
       vulnerabilities in the Tasks Android app, not in Kotlin coroutines.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      False positive: kotlinx-coroutines-play-services is a Kotlin coroutines
      integration library for Google Play Services.  The NVD CPE
      cpe:2.3:a:tasks:tasks: matches by artifact-name substring ("tasks" appears
      in the org.jetbrains.kotlinx groupId path) and the version number.  The CVEs
      CVE-2020-22475 and CVE-2022-39349 are vulnerabilities in the Tasks Android
      productivity application (tasks.org), which is a completely unrelated project.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlinx:kotlinx-coroutines-play-services:.*$</gav>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:tasks:tasks</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       NOT ACTIONABLE (embedded in Android test-tooling JAR):
       Netty 4.1.72.Final inside core-0.0.9-alpha02.jar
       ======================================================================
       The file core-0.0.9-alpha02.jar is part of the Android Test Orchestrator /
       device-provider tooling downloaded by AGP.  It embeds Netty 4.1.72.Final
       in its META-INF/maven/ tree.  We have no control over this JAR's contents.
       Our own Netty dependency is forced to 4.1.137.Final via resolutionStrategy.
       These findings will resolve automatically when Google ships an updated
       version of the Android test tooling (0.0.9-alpha02 → a newer release).
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      Not actionable: Netty 4.1.72.Final is embedded inside core-0.0.9-alpha02.jar,
      which is an Android test-tooling artifact managed by AGP.  This JAR is only
      used during test execution (not shipped in the production APK).  Our
      resolutionStrategy forces all directly resolved Netty jars to 4.1.137.Final,
      but force() cannot reach into embedded JARs.  Re-evaluate when the Android
      test tooling is updated to a version that embeds a patched Netty.
    </notes>
    <filePath regex="true">.*core-0\.0\.9-alpha02\.jar.*</filePath>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:netty:netty</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       NOT ACTIONABLE (embedded in Android test-tooling JAR):
       Guava 28.1-jre inside android-device-provider-local-0.0.9-alpha02.jar
       ======================================================================
       Same situation as core-0.0.9-alpha02.jar above.  This artifact is part of
       the Android device-provider test tooling and only used during test execution.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      Not actionable: Guava 28.1-jre is embedded inside
      android-device-provider-local-0.0.9-alpha02.jar, an Android test-tooling
      artifact managed by AGP.  Not shipped in the production APK.  Our
      resolutionStrategy forces all directly resolved Guava jars to 33.6.0.
      Re-evaluate when Google ships updated device-provider tooling.
    </notes>
    <filePath regex="true">.*android-device-provider-local-0\.0\.9-alpha02\.jar.*</filePath>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:google:guava</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       NOT ACTIONABLE (embedded in Android test-tooling JAR):
       Protobuf-kotlin 3.18.0 inside launcher-0.0.9-alpha02.jar
       ======================================================================
       launcher-0.0.9-alpha02.jar is an Android test orchestrator launcher JAR
