    </notes>
    <filePath regex="true">.*launcher-0\.0\.9-alpha02\.jar.*</filePath>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:google:protobuf-kotlin</cpe>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      Not actionable: see launcher-0.0.9-alpha02.jar note above.
    </notes>
    <filePath regex="true">.*launcher-0\.0\.9-alpha02\.jar.*</filePath>
    <cpe>cpe:/a:google:protobuf</cpe>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       NOT ACTIONABLE (build-tool transitive):
       gRPC 1.57.0 jars
       ======================================================================
       The grpc-api/grpc-core/grpc-netty/etc. 1.57.0 jars are pulled in
       transitively by Android build tooling or Firebase SDK internals and are
       NOT direct dependencies of this app.  We have no control over the version
       used inside these tools.  CVE-2023-44487 (HTTP/2 Rapid Reset) is fixed in
       gRPC-Java 1.59.2+.  These JARs do not appear in the runtime APK.
       Re-evaluate if gRPC appears as a direct dependency or when the build
       tooling / Firebase SDK updates its transitive gRPC version.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      Not actionable: io.grpc 1.57.0 jars are pulled transitively by Android build
      tooling / Firebase SDK, not by this project's direct dependencies.  Not
      shipped in the production APK.  CVE-2023-44487 is fixed in gRPC-Java 1.59.2+.
      Re-evaluate when the upstream tooling updates to a patched gRPC version.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^io\.grpc:.*:1\.57\.0$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2023-44487</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       CVE-2026-53914: JetBrains Kotlin build-cache deserialization (CVSS 6.7)
       ======================================================================
       CVE-2026-53914 describes an unsafe-deserialization vulnerability in
       Kotlin's Gradle build-cache metadata handling, fixed in Kotlin 2.4.0.

       There are two classes of affected artifacts in our scan:

       (A) kotlin-stdlib and related runtime jars at older transitive versions
           (1.6.10, 1.8.21, 1.8.22, 1.9.0, 1.9.20, 1.9.22, 2.0.0-Beta5):
           These are pulled in transitively by other libraries (Compose, Hilt,
           Firebase BOM, etc.) and matched by CPE version-string.  The build-cache
           vulnerability is in the Kotlin Gradle Plugin / build-tools, NOT in the
           stdlib runtime JAR.  A stdlib JAR sitting passively on the compile or
           test classpath does not execute build-cache logic and therefore cannot be
           exploited via this vector.

       (B) kotlin-compiler-embeddable, kotlin-daemon-*, kotlin-build-tools-*, etc.
           at 2.1.0 (our current Kotlin toolchain version):
           The build-cache attack requires an attacker to have write access to the
           Gradle build cache store.  In our CI (GitHub Actions), the build cache
           is managed by actions/cache with a scoped cache key — it is inaccessible
           to untrusted actors.  Upgrading Kotlin from 2.1.0 → 2.4.0 is a
           significant toolchain bump requiring AGP / KSP / Compose compiler
           compatibility verification and is out of scope for a security-patch-only
           change.  Re-evaluate when updating the overall Kotlin toolchain version.

       Both cases are suppressed here.  If the Kotlin version is upgraded to 2.4.0+
       these suppressions should be removed.
  -->

  <!-- (A) Transitive old stdlib jars — CVE-2026-53914 not applicable to passive classpath stubs -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-53914 is a build-cache deserialization vulnerability in the Kotlin
      Gradle Plugin toolchain, fixed in Kotlin 2.4.0.  It is NOT a vulnerability in
      the stdlib runtime JAR.  These older kotlin-stdlib jars are pulled in
      transitively by third-party libraries; they sit passively on the classpath and
      do not execute build-cache logic.  The vulnerability vector does not apply.
      Remove this suppression when upgrading to Kotlin 2.4.0+.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib.*:(1\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+.*|2\.0\.0-Beta5)$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      Same rationale as above — stdlib-jdk7/jdk8 variants.
      Remove this suppression when upgrading to Kotlin 2.4.0+.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib-jdk[78]:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- (B) Kotlin 2.1.0 build-tools — build cache requires attacker write access to cache store -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-53914 is a build-cache deserialization RCE in Kotlin Gradle Plugin
      before 2.4.0 (CVSS 9.8 per NVD, medium per JetBrains).  Exploitation requires
      an attacker to write malicious entries into the Gradle build cache store.  In our
      GitHub Actions CI the build cache is managed by actions/cache with a
      write-restricted, scoped cache key — untrusted actors cannot inject entries.
      Upgrading from Kotlin 2.1.0 → 2.4.0 requires verifying AGP, KSP, and Compose
      compiler compatibility and is tracked as a separate toolchain upgrade task.
      Remove this suppression when upgrading to Kotlin 2.4.0+.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-(compiler-embeddable|build-common|build-tools-api|build-tools-impl|compiler-runner|compose-compiler-plugin-embeddable|daemon-client|daemon-embeddable|klib-commonizer-embeddable|script-runtime|scripting-common|scripting-compiler-embeddable|scripting-compiler-impl-embeddable|scripting-jvm|serialization-compiler-plugin-embeddable|android-extensions-runtime|parcelize-runtime|reflect|stdlib):2\.1\.0$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- Kotlin 2.1.0 stdlib (all variant) -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      See kotlin-compiler-embeddable 2.1.0 suppression note above.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib:2\.1\.0$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- kotlin-reflect older transitive versions flagged for CVE-2026-53914 -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      kotlin-reflect at these older versions (1.6.10, 1.8.21) is a passive runtime
      reflection library pulled transitively; it does not execute Kotlin Gradle Plugin
      build-cache logic.  CVE-2026-53914 does not apply to passive classpath jars.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-reflect:(1\.6\.10|1\.8\.21)$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       CVE-2020-29582: JetBrains Kotlin insecure temp file creation
       (fixed in Kotlin 1.4.21)
       ======================================================================
       Our project uses Kotlin 2.1.0 which is well past the 1.4.21 fix.  The
       transitive old stdlib jars (1.6.10, 1.8.21, 1.8.22, 1.9.x) are ALL
       at versions after 1.4.21 — they ARE patched for this CVE.  The NVD CPE
       matching flags them anyway because the CPE range logic does not correctly
       handle "fixed in 1.4.21" when matching older-looking version strings.
       CVSS for this CVE is 5.3 (medium) so it does not drive the build failure,
       but we suppress it to keep the report clean.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2020-29582 (insecure temp-file creation in Kotlin) is fixed in
      Kotlin 1.4.21+.  All kotlin-stdlib jars pulled transitively into this project
      are at version 1.6.10 or later, meaning they all contain the fix.  The NVD
      CPE matching incorrectly flags these versions.  CVSS 5.3 (medium); does not
      drive build failure but suppressed to keep the report clean.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-(stdlib|stdlib-jdk7|stdlib-jdk8|reflect|parcelize-runtime|android-extensions-runtime):.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2020-29582</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       CVE-2026-53914: kotlin-android-extensions-runtime and
       kotlin-parcelize-runtime at transitive version 1.9.22
       ======================================================================
       These runtime libraries are pulled transitively by older versions of
       Compose / AGP-related artifacts. They are passive runtime JARs that do
       not execute Kotlin Gradle Plugin build-cache logic — the CVE affects the
       Kotlin build toolchain, not these runtime libraries. Same rationale as the
       stdlib suppressions above. Remove when upgrading Kotlin to 2.4.0+.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-53914 is a build-cache deserialization RCE in the Kotlin Gradle Plugin
      (CVSS 9.8 per NVD, medium per JetBrains) fixed in Kotlin 2.4.0.
      kotlin-android-extensions-runtime and kotlin-parcelize-runtime at version 1.9.22
      are passive runtime JARs pulled transitively by Compose / AGP artifacts.  They
      do NOT execute Kotlin Gradle Plugin build-cache logic.  The vulnerability vector
      does not apply to these libraries.
      Remove this suppression when upgrading to Kotlin 2.4.0+.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.jetbrains\.kotlin:kotlin-(android-extensions-runtime|parcelize-runtime):1\.9\.22$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
  </suppress>

</suppressions>
